content.thinking:
The bug is at line 509: `var rooms = Array.isArray(data && data.rooms) ? data.rooms : [];` — this treats malformed responses as empty list. Need to distinguish: HTTP 200 + JSON parseable + top-level object + rooms is array → success; otherwise → error message.

Note: `data && data.rooms` — if data is null, `data && data.rooms` is null → not array → []. If data is an array, `data.rooms` is undefined → []. Need to throw error in those cases.

Fix: in the `.then(function (data) {...})`, validate:

```js
.then(function (data) {
  if (seq !== listQuerySeq) return;
  var valid = data !== null && typeof data === 'object' && !Array.isArray(data) &&
    Array.isArray(data.rooms);
  if (!valid) throw ... // but need to not throw past the seq check
```

Careful: the seq check must happen before deciding. If we throw after seq check, the catch will check seq again — fine, since seq === listQuerySeq still. So:

```js
.then(function (data) {
  if (seq !== listQuerySeq) return;
  if (data === null || typeof data !== 'object' || Array.isArray(data) || !Array.isArray(data.rooms)) {
    throw new Error('bad list format');
  }
  renderRooms(data.rooms);
})
```

The catch already renders the error message and checks seq. That works — a stale malformed response: seq !== listQuerySeq → return before validation, ignored. Good.

Also note: resp.ok check — "查询返回 HTTP 200 且正文能解析为 JSON 时" — resp.ok is 200-299. The spec says HTTP 200. Existing code uses `!resp.ok` throw. Keep it. Actually spec says "查询返回 HTTP 200 且正文能解析为 JSON 时，只有顶层是 JSON 对象、且 rooms 字段是数组，才能按读取成功展示" — the existing resp.ok check is fine.

Also "不展示旧表格冒充最新结果" — the catch clears listArea.innerHTML, good.

Also check the create flow: after create success, `return loadRooms()` — if loadRooms fails, the error message shows in list area, form message stays as success. The `.finally` re-enables button. Good — no changes needed there since loadRooms catches its own errors.

Let me also check tests to see expected behavior. Let me look at ui.test.mjs or similar to see if there's a test for this. Let me quickly check test files for the relevant expectations.

